window.JG_DB["Briar"] = {"Bel'Veth":{"tldr":"Bel'Veth adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Bel'Veth seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Bel'Veth attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Bel'Veth into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Bel'Veth's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Bel'Veth or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Bel'Veth's first item turns the dash chain into sustained damage — she stops trading and starts running people down."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Bel'Veth is even with you at levels 1 and 2, because Void Surge dashes let her step out of Blood Frenzy while Royal Maelstrom heals her through your bleed. At level 3 Head Rush (475 range) stuns her in place and your healing pulls ahead, so plan your fight for then. Start red and full clear toward the scuttle nearest your mid. If she reaches you before level 3, trade once and leave instead of frenzying into her. Above and Below (12-second cooldown) knocks you up out of a chase, so bait it before you commit. Recall after the level-3 crab fight.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Bel'Veth is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Bel'Veth takes scuttle quickly with Death in Lavender attack speed and can dash out of the contest the moment it turns.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Bel'Veth if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Bel'Veth wants every Void Grub and Rift Herald for the coral, because true form is what her whole game is built on.","invade":"Walk into Bel'Veth's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Bel'Veth holds four charges of escape, so an invade only works if you cut the dash line rather than chase it.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Count her Void Surge charges — with all four spent she is a melee champion with no way out of the pit.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Bel'Veth's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Bel'Veth is weakest before she banks a coral, when her health pool is small and her stacks have not built.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Bel'Veth takes side waves happily, because the attack-speed stacks make her a fast pusher as well as a duellist.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Bel'Veth picks come from dashing through a wall onto someone already slowed, so watch the terrain behind you.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Bel'Veth wins by banking a coral early, entering true form on an objective, and stacking through a fight nobody can end quickly."},"Diana":{"tldr":"Diana adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Diana seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Diana attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Diana into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Diana's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Diana or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Diana's first item turns the Q-dash-Moonfall rotation from a chunk into a kill on anything without an escape."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Diana has no burst before Lunar Rush and her clear is slow, so you beat her at every early level. Start red, clear two camps and walk into her jungle at level 3, when Head Rush plus Blood Frenzy can kill her before Pale Cascade's shield does anything. Crescent Strike (900 range, 8-second cooldown) is her only way to set up the dash, so frenzy in after the moonbeam has been thrown. Both scuttles are yours too, since Pale Cascade cannot out-trade a frenzy. Recall with her camps in your pocket, and ward her blue so you catch her again on her second clear.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Diana is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Diana contests scuttle with Crescent Strike poke rather than a fight, and commits only once Lunar Rush is up.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Diana if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Diana takes objectives quickly with the passive triple-strike, but her smite fight is weak until her ultimate is online.","invade":"Walk into Diana's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Diana can only dash to something she has marked, so invading before Crescent Strike lands takes away her escape.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. The whole kit keys off Crescent Strike — if the arc misses, the dash and the pull are both off the table.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Diana's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Diana is weakest before six, when her clear is excellent and her kill threat genuinely is not.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Diana pushes a side lane very fast off her passive and is a real threat to anyone who answers it alone.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Diana picks are a Moonfall pull on someone standing near a wall, which is why she wants the fight in a corridor.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Diana wins by reaching six and two items and then one-rotating whichever squishy steps a pace too far forward."},"Ekko":{"tldr":"Ekko adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Ekko seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Ekko attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Ekko into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Ekko's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Ekko or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Ekko's first item is the point where his dive stops being a trade and becomes a kill, with the rewind as insurance."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Ekko pays health for his clear and has nothing to stop a Briar who has already started frenzying, so you beat him at every early level. Full clear to level 3, then invade the camp he finishes on. Parallel Convergence (22-second cooldown) is the one thing that punishes you, because Blood Frenzy will run you straight into the stun ring, so cancel the frenzy with Chilling Scream if you see it forming. Phase Dive (325 range) is his only escape; Head Rush follows it easily. Take the scuttle on his side while he is still healing from the clear, then recall.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Ekko is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Ekko wants the scuttle fight only if Parallel Convergence is already drawn on the crab — without the stun he backs off.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Ekko if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Ekko is a poor early smite fighter, so objectives before six are usually contestable if you arrive with health.","invade":"Walk into Ekko's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Ekko holds Phase Dive and Chronobreak, so a successful invade needs to land before six or with both of those tracked.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Watch for the Parallel Convergence ring on the ground — everything he does afterwards is timed to that stun.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Ekko's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Ekko is weakest between three and six, when his clear costs health and Chronobreak is not there to undo a mistake.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Ekko is one of the better side laners in the jungle, because he can dive the wave and rewind out of the answer.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Ekko picks come from a W stun placed behind you in a choke, so cross open ground rather than corridors when he is missing.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Ekko wins by taking dives nobody else can take and rewinding out of the punish until the lead compounds."},"Elise":{"tldr":"Elise adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Elise seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Elise attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Elise into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Elise's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Elise or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Elise's first item keeps the spider-form burst relevant a while longer, but it is the last window where it one-shots."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Elise loses to you at levels 1 and 2, and at level 3 Cocoon (1075 range) and Rappel make it an even fight. Start on the side facing her first buff and invade at level 2, before she has both. If Cocoon stuns you mid-frenzy, you will still chase her, so hold W until the Cocoon has been thrown. Rappel makes her untargetable, which ends Blood Frenzy early, so use Head Rush after she lands. Take the scuttle at level 2 if you can reach it. Recall after full clear, and ward her raptors to track her level-3 gank.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Elise is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Elise contests scuttle hard — a landed Cocoon at that timer is usually a kill and not just a crab.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Elise if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Elise has poor objective damage for her power level, so a drake she takes alone is slow and interruptible.","invade":"Walk into Elise's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Elise escapes an invade with Rappel, which makes her untargetable, so the punish has to land before that E is up.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Cocoon is the whole matchup — if it misses, spider form has to walk into you with no way back out.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Elise's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Elise is weakest after the mid game, when the Cocoon still lands but the burst behind it stops killing.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Elise does not side lane; she wants to be near her team, where a pick turns straight into an objective.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Elise picks are a Cocoon from a bush at a river entrance, so sweep before you cross and never walk the same line twice.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Elise wins by cashing her level-three and mid-game power into objectives before her damage falls behind."},"Evelynn":{"tldr":"Evelynn adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Evelynn seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Evelynn attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Evelynn into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Evelynn's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Evelynn or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Evelynn's first item plus camouflage is the spike that flips the matchup — the charm rotation starts killing outright."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Evelynn is the weakest early jungler in the game and cannot survive a Blood Frenzy before level 6. Start on the side facing her first buff, clear two camps and invade her raptors or second buff at level 3. Allure (15-second cooldown) only charms after its delay, so Head Rush onto her and frenzy before she can wait it out. Take the scuttles as well; she has no way to contest them before six. Recall after taking her camps, and ward her blue before six, when Demon Shade lets her walk up to you unseen.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Evelynn is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Evelynn will not contest a scuttle before six unless she has numbers — an unstealthed Evelynn loses that fight.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Evelynn if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Evelynn cannot solo objectives early, so anything before her ultimate is a timer you can take with confidence.","invade":"Walk into Evelynn's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Evelynn is the best invade target in the jungle before six; after six she simply is not there to be invaded.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. From six on, treat every unswept bush as occupied — the charm is the start of everything she does.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Evelynn's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Evelynn is weakest from one to five, and it is not close; this matchup is decided by how hard you punish that.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Evelynn does not hold a side lane, she hunts one — a laner alone on that side is the bait, not the answer.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Evelynn picks are a charm out of camouflage onto whoever walked without a sweeper, and that is the whole late game.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Evelynn wins by surviving to six, then removing one person per fight before the fight has properly started."},"Graves":{"tldr":"Graves adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Graves seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Graves attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Graves into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Graves's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Graves or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Graves' first item is a large step in raw damage — the double-shot at point blank starts removing squishies outright."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Graves beats you at level 1 because his shotgun autos stop your healing from mattering; at level 2 it is even, and from level 3 Head Rush and frenzy healing win. Open on the buff away from his first camp and clear all six. End of the Line (925 range, 13-second cooldown) and Quickdraw are his burst, so wait for both before you frenzy in. Smoke Screen cuts your vision, but Blood Frenzy keeps you chasing him anyway. Meet him at the level-3 scuttle and recall after that fight. Ward his raptors, the camp he takes when he invades.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Graves is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Graves takes scuttle fast and wins the contest at point-blank range, where both shells of a reload land on you.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Graves if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Graves is an excellent objective duellist because Smoke Screen blinds your smite fight and his burst is front-loaded.","invade":"Walk into Graves's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Invade Graves in the open rather than in his buff pit, because True Grit armour makes him the stronger side of a close-quarters brawl.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Count his shells: a Graves mid-reload has no burst, and that is the only safe second to step into him.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Graves's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Graves is weakest in open ground at range, where his pellets spread and he cannot make the auto-attacks count.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Graves is a strong side laner who holds a wave against most of the map and pushes it fast when left alone.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Graves picks come from a Smoke Screen dropped on a choke, so never walk a corridor he already has vision of.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Graves wins by taking your camps, holding a side lane, and shredding anyone who answers him in a tight space."},"Kayn":{"tldr":"Kayn adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Kayn seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Kayn attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Kayn into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Kayn's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Kayn or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Kayn's first item lands around the same time as his form, which is why that window is a sharp jump and not a slope."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Kayn is formless and farming orbs, and your frenzy healing beats him at every early level. Full clear, then invade the camp he finished at around level 3, when Reaping Slash has left him low. Shadow Step (21-second cooldown) lets him walk through a wall to escape, and Blood Frenzy cannot follow him inside terrain, so fight him in open jungle. Blade's Reach (700 range) slows you, so Head Rush in after it has been used. Take every scuttle before he has a form, and recall after the invade.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Kayn is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Kayn contests scuttle only when the orb count needs it — before a form he would rather take the safe crab.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Kayn if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Kayn is a weak early objective fighter, so pre-form pits are a timer you can take against him.","invade":"Walk into Kayn's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Kayn walks out of any invade through a wall with Shadow Step, so the only punish is catching him mid-camp.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. The form is the clock: check which orbs he is taking, because that decides whether he brawls or bursts.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Kayn's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Kayn is weakest pre-form, when his stats lag every jungler on the roster and his kit is only mobility.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Kayn side lanes very well once formed, and the wall-walk means answering him alone rarely ends with a kill.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Kayn picks come out of a wall you did not ward, so treat every piece of terrain near him as an entrance.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Kayn wins by surviving to his form and then either bursting your carry or brawling through your front line."},"Kha'Zix":{"tldr":"Kha'Zix adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Kha'Zix seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Kha'Zix attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Kha'Zix into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Kha'Zix's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Kha'Zix or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Kha'Zix's first item plus the first evolution is the spike — an isolated squishy stops surviving the opener."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Kha'Zix hits isolated targets hard, but you heal off every hit and win the early fight at all three levels. Full clear and meet him at scuttle, where Taste Their Fear (4-second cooldown) is his only real damage. Leap (700 range) is his escape, so Head Rush him before he can use it. Blood Frenzy follows him through Leap unless he lands over a wall. Invade his raptors at level 3 if your mid can follow. Recall after the crab, and ward his blue so you know which side he evolves on.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Kha'Zix is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Kha'Zix contests scuttle happily if you are alone at it, because the isolation bonus turns the crab into a kill.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Kha'Zix if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Kha'Zix has strong single-target objective damage but a poor pit fight against anyone with crowd control.","invade":"Walk into Kha'Zix's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Kha'Zix escapes an invade with Leap and, once evolved, with the ultimate's stealth, so cut the escape angle first.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Isolation is the whole thing — near a camp or an ally his Q does far less, so never face-check alone.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Kha'Zix's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Kha'Zix is weakest in a grouped fight, where nothing is isolated and his burst has no preferred target.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Kha'Zix side lanes to look for a lone answer rather than to push, so the wave is bait as often as not.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Kha'Zix picks are an evolved leap onto whoever walked a corridor alone, which is why vision on side entrances matters.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Kha'Zix wins by finding an isolated target every fight and deleting it before the fight is joined."},"Kindred":{"tldr":"Kindred adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Kindred seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Kindred attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Kindred into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Kindred's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Kindred or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Kindred's first item plus a few stacks is where the ranged trade stops being poke and starts being a duel they win."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Kindred wants to kite you with Dance of Arrows, but a Head Rush stun and a frenzy that keeps chasing win every early fight you start close enough. Kindred's monster marks bring them into your jungle, so full clear toward the camp that gets marked and wait there. Dance of Arrows (9-second cooldown) is their only dash; once it has been used, Blood Frenzy runs them down. Mounting Dread bursts on the third hit, so finish the fight before it stacks. Take the first scuttle, and recall once you have killed Kindred or taken the mark.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Kindred is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Kindred wins scuttle contests by kiting rather than fighting — three dashes banked means the crab is theirs.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Kindred if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Kindred takes objectives quickly with the passive attack speed and can hold a pit with Lamb's Respite.","invade":"Walk into Kindred's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Kindred is hard to catch in an invade, since every Q is a dash and the jungle terrain works in their favour.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Watch the mark: a live mark on your side of the map says exactly where Kindred is going next.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Kindred's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Kindred is weakest with no marks stacked and no dashes banked, which is when their damage is simply low.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Kindred side lanes safely because the kiting pattern beats anything that has to walk at them.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Kindred does not pick so much as collect, so the danger is chasing them into a Lamb's Respite you cannot leave.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Kindred wins by stacking marks early and turning every late fight into a kite their team fights inside."},"Lee Sin":{"tldr":"Lee Sin adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Lee Sin seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Lee Sin attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Lee Sin into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Lee Sin's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Lee Sin or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Lee Sin's first item is his last real jump — after it his damage stays flat while everyone else keeps climbing."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Lee Sin is ahead of you at levels 1 and 2 and even at level 3. Sonic Wave (1100 range, 10-second cooldown) pulls him onto you, and Safeguard gets him out when your healing starts to win. He likes to invade at level 2 or 3, so ward your raptors and start on the side your laners cover. Let him have the scuttle while you are still level 2. Once you have Chilling Scream charged, you can stand your ground at 3: a knock-back into a wall stuns him. Recall after the full clear, and fight him when Safeguard has been used.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Lee Sin is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Lee Sin fights for every scuttle — the Q re-cast plus Flurry resets are at their strongest at exactly that timer.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Lee Sin if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Lee Sin is a strong early objective contester because Dragon's Rage can kick you out of the pit entirely.","invade":"Walk into Lee Sin's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Invade Lee Sin with his energy spent, because ward-hops let him reach — and leave — camps you did not expect him at.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Everything starts with Sonic Wave — stand behind a camp so it cannot connect and half his kit is idle.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Lee Sin's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Lee Sin is weakest from two items on, when his burst stops killing and his utility is all that is left.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Lee Sin side lanes poorly late; he wants the mid game, where a kick decides a fight before it starts.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Lee Sin picks are a Q from fog into a kick that separates you from your team, so hold your dash for the second hit.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Lee Sin wins by converting an early lead into objectives before the two-item mark takes his damage away."},"Naafiri":{"tldr":"Naafiri adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Naafiri seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Naafiri attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Naafiri into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Naafiri's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Naafiri or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Naafiri's first item is where the dagger bleed plus the pack becomes a full health bar rather than a heavy trade."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Naafiri's packmates are the first thing Blood Frenzy hits if you do not aim it, and your bleed damage kills them quickly, so you win every early fight. Full clear on your strong side, then invade her raptors at level 3. Darkin Daggers (900 range, 9-second cooldown) is her poke; Head Rush onto Naafiri herself so the frenzy locks onto her, not a dog. Hounds' Pursuit is her escape, and you can follow it. Take the first scuttle and recall after the invade, with a ward on her blue.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Naafiri is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Naafiri wins a scuttle contest on numbers — the dogs make a level-two or level-three crab fight a 3v1.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Naafiri if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Naafiri has solid single-target objective damage but no way to hold a pit against a champion with a knock-up.","invade":"Walk into Naafiri's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Naafiri answers an invade with Hounds' Pursuit, which is untargetable, so kill the packmates before you commit.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Count the dogs — a Naafiri with no packmates up has lost most of her damage until they respawn.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Naafiri's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Naafiri is weakest with the pack dead, which is why clearing them first changes the fight more than any cooldown.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Naafiri side lanes fast and is a genuine 1v1 threat, but she gives up the fight around objectives to do it.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Naafiri picks are a W dash onto anyone she can already reach with a slow, so break the slow before the dash lands.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Naafiri wins by picking one target per fight and having the pack finish it before your team can rotate."},"Nidalee":{"tldr":"Nidalee adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Nidalee seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Nidalee attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Nidalee into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Nidalee's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Nidalee or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Nidalee's first item makes the spear a genuine execute threat rather than chip damage on the way to a fight."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Nidalee pokes from 1500 range with Javelin Toss, but she cannot out-heal your bleed and dies to one frenzy. You win every early fight. Full clear with a ward in the river brush near your raptors, because she comes looking for a spear hit. When she throws and misses, Head Rush onto her; Pounce will not carry her out of a frenzy. Take the first scuttle, and invade her blue once you have seen her top side. Recall after taking her blue.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Nidalee is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Nidalee decides scuttle contests with a max-range Javelin before either of you is standing on the crab.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Nidalee if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Nidalee has excellent objective damage from the hunt bonus but cannot hold a pit against a real duellist.","invade":"Walk into Nidalee's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Nidalee cannot be caught in an invade — the pounce reset means she leaves through terrain you cannot follow.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. The Javelin is the tell: a landed spear means the pounce is coming, so break line of sight instead of walking back.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Nidalee's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Nidalee is weakest at close range with her cooldowns spent, where a cougar with no pounce has to fight honestly.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Nidalee does not hold a side lane; she poke-clears it and leaves before anyone can arrive.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Nidalee picks are a spear out of fog followed by a pounce, which is why the spear line matters more than her position.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Nidalee wins by poking a target below the hunt threshold and executing it before the fight begins properly."},"Nocturne":{"tldr":"Nocturne is a melee dive threat, not a kiter: Shroud of Darkness (W) can eat your Head Rush stun on a fade-out bait, Unspeakable Horror (E) fears you off a target if you can't close the gap in time, and Paranoia (R) lets him pick a target from range with a blind-vision global dash. Briar answers with Head Rush (Q) to shred his armor and lock him down, Blood Frenzy (W) to run him down once the fear ends, and Certain Death (R) for her own cross-map dive. Nocturne wants to snowball off his passive Umbra Blades sustain and land a fear-into-burst window; he does not out-kite you, so play around when his spell shield and fear are down, not around chasing a runner.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Nocturne attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Nocturne into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Nocturne's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Nocturne or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Nocturne's first item is where the Duskbringer trade stops being a chunk and becomes a kill on any squishy."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Nocturne clears quickly and has Unspeakable Horror to fear you, but before level 6 your frenzy healing beats him at every level. Full clear and fight him at scuttle, where his Duskbringer trail gives him nothing to hide in. Shroud of Darkness (20-second cooldown) blocks your Head Rush stun, so let him spend it on a camp or bait it with Chilling Scream first. The fear tether breaks if you walk out of range, but Blood Frenzy keeps you close, so kill him before it lands. Invade his raptors at level 3. Recall after the fight and ward his blue before Paranoia comes online.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Nocturne is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Nocturne contests scuttle on the Duskbringer trail, where the movement speed and the fear make the trade one-sided.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Nocturne if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Nocturne is a good single-target objective taker with the passive heal but has no zone control in the pit.","invade":"Walk into Nocturne's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Nocturne's spell shield makes an invade awkward — bait it with a low-value ability before committing the real one.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Watch the spell shield: while it is up your engage is refunded, and while it is down he is an ordinary melee.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Nocturne's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Nocturne is weakest against a team that stays grouped, since the fear tether breaks on distance and needs isolation.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Nocturne side lanes well and threatens to leave it at any moment, because his ultimate reaches the whole map.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Nocturne picks are a Paranoia dive onto someone he has already chunked, so hug terrain near allies on the cast.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Nocturne wins by darkening the map and arriving on the one person your team cannot afford to lose."},"Rengar":{"tldr":"Rengar adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Rengar seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Rengar attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Rengar into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Rengar's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Rengar or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Rengar's first item is the point where an empowered Savagery stops chunking and starts one-shotting squishier targets."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Rengar is even with you at level 1 because Unseen Predator gives him a free leap from brush, but from level 2 your frenzy healing wins. Clear, then fight him over scuttle in the open river, where Unseen Predator has no bush to use. Bola Strike (1000 range) roots at full ferocity, and Battle Roar cleanses your stun if he has four ferocity stacks, so wait for him to spend them. Invade his raptors at level 3 when he has been seen on the other side. Recall after the scuttle fight and ward the brush near your camps.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Rengar is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Rengar contests scuttle from a brush — a leap opener at that timer is usually a kill rather than a trade.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Rengar if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Rengar has good single-target objective damage but nothing that holds a pit if the fight goes long.","invade":"Walk into Rengar's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Rengar invades through brush lines, so the bushes on your side of the jungle are the ones that matter.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. The ferocity count is the tell — at four stacks the next ability is the empowered one, and that is the burst.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Rengar's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Rengar is weakest in the middle of an open corridor, where there is no bush to open from and no reset to chain.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Rengar side lanes to hunt whoever answers rather than to push, so treat the wave as bait until proven otherwise.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Rengar picks are a stealth leap out of Thrill of the Hunt, so control wards do more for you than health does.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Rengar wins by removing a squishy at the start of every fight from a bush your team did not sweep."},"Shaco":{"tldr":"Shaco adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Shaco seeks to vanish with Deceive (Q) to slip your frenzy rather than kite it, bait you onto a Jack in the Box (W) fear, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Shaco attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Shaco into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Shaco's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Shaco or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Shaco's first item is where the Deceive opener plus box damage becomes a one-rotation kill on squishier targets."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Shaco invades level 1 with Jack In The Box plants and wins that first fight, because Blood Frenzy will chase you straight into the boxes. At level 2 it is even and from level 3 you win. Ward the buff you want to start before camps spawn, and switch sides if the ward finds boxes. Deceive (13-second cooldown) is his escape; wait until he has blinked in before you Head Rush. Do not frenzy near unwarded brush. Take the level-3 scuttle and recall after full clear.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Shaco is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Shaco contests scuttle with boxes already down, which makes the crab a 3v1 rather than a duel.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Shaco if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Shaco has strong single-target objective damage off Backstab but folds in a pit fight he cannot open from stealth.","invade":"Walk into Shaco's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Shaco invades level one more than almost anyone, so the fear is the boxes at your buff rather than the champion.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Boxes are the map: a cleared box line tells you exactly which entrance he intends to fight at.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Shaco's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Shaco is weakest in an even fight with no boxes and no clone, which is the only version worth taking.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Shaco side lanes to threaten a backdoor rather than to duel, and the clone makes answering him a guess.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Shaco picks are a Deceive from behind onto someone alone, so keep a wall at your back near his side of the map.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Shaco wins by making every second of the game confusing and cashing one clean pick per fight."},"Talon":{"tldr":"Talon adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Talon seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, vault over terrain with Assassin's Path (E) to break your frenzy's line rather than kite it, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Talon attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Talon into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Talon's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Talon or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Talon's first item is the point where the bleed rotation goes from a heavy chunk to a full kill on a squishy."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Talon has no crowd control, and you win at levels 1 and 2; at level 3 Head Rush plus frenzy healing beats his burst easily. Full clear and meet him at scuttle, or catch him when he hops a wall into your jungle. Noxian Diplomacy (575 range, 8-second cooldown) is his burst, and Chilling Scream reduces the damage while you heal. Assassin's Path lets him escape over walls, so stun him before he reaches one. Invade his raptors at level 3, and ward the wall-hop spots near your camps. Recall once his raptors are gone.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Talon is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Talon contests scuttle by arriving over a wall you did not expect, and leaves the same way if it turns.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Talon if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Talon has decent single-target objective damage but no way to hold a pit against anyone with crowd control.","invade":"Walk into Talon's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Talon cannot really be trapped — Assassin's Path takes him over terrain no chase can follow.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Track his wall-hop cooldowns per wall: a wall he has just crossed is one he cannot cross again immediately.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Talon's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Talon is weakest in a grouped fight, where the burst has no isolated target and the stealth has nowhere to end.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Talon side lanes to find a solo kill and rotate over walls, so he is a threat to two lanes at once.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Talon picks are a wall-hop into a full rotation on whoever is furthest forward, so never be that person.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Talon wins by removing an isolated carry and leaving over terrain before anyone can trade back."},"Viego":{"tldr":"Viego adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Viego seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Viego attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Viego into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Viego's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) gives you a long-range global initiation and a fear on arrival, but it grants no CC-immunity — if you're already low, Viego's Heartbreaker (R) is an execute that can end the fight the instant he closes the gap. Time the cast from fog of war onto an isolated target rather than assuming you're untouchable once you land. This is your biggest mechanical spike and turns you into a real map-wide threat, provided you land it above his execute threshold."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Viego's first item is where the sustained damage becomes a duel he wins outright rather than a trade he survives."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Viego heals with Blade of the Ruined King, but your frenzy heals more and you win at every early level. Full clear, then fight him for the scuttle before a takedown lets him possess anyone. Spectral Maw (8-second cooldown) stuns you only if he charges it, and Blood Frenzy runs you right into it, so Head Rush him first to interrupt the charge. Harrowed Path mist makes him hard to see near walls, so ward your raptors and blue entrances. Walk into his raptors at level 3 when a laner can follow your frenzy. Recall once you have the crab, before his first takedown gives him a reset.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Viego is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Viego contests scuttle with the Spectral Maw stun, and the crab fight is decided by whether that charge lands.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Viego if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Viego is a good objective duellist with sustained damage but has no way to zone you off the pit.","invade":"Walk into Viego's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Viego escapes an invade through Harrowed Path, so the mist trails on the map are the routes he actually uses.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Dodge the Maw charge-up — without the stun his early all-in is a set of ordinary auto-attacks.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Viego's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Viego is weakest in a fight where nothing dies, since every reset he gets depends on a body being available.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Viego side lanes well and the possession makes answering him with one person risky if a wave is dying nearby.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Viego picks come out of the mist onto someone already low, so treat any mist trail as an occupied corridor.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Viego wins by turning one won fight into three through resets, which is why the first kill matters most."},"Wukong":{"tldr":"Wukong adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Wukong seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Wukong attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Wukong into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Wukong's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) gives you a long-range global initiation and a fear on arrival — Wukong carries no hard CC of his own, so a clean landing is genuinely hard for him to answer directly. His counterplay is repositioning, not lockdown: Warrior Trickster (W) can stealth him out of your fear radius, and Cyclone (R) knocks up anyone caught in it if he turns to fight. Time the cast from fog of war onto an isolated target and this is your biggest mechanical spike of the game."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Wukong's first item is where the armour shred plus Crushing Blow becomes a duel he wins rather than survives."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Wukong's Warrior Trickster clone is the one trick that beats you: Blood Frenzy locks onto the nearest enemy, and the nearest enemy is often the clone. You still win every early fight if you aim Head Rush at the real Wukong first. Full clear and meet him at the level-3 scuttle. Nimbus Strike (650 range) is his dash; stun him when he lands. Warrior Trickster (22-second cooldown) also makes him invisible, so wait for him to reappear before committing. Invade his raptors when your lanes are pushed, and recall after the crab.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Wukong is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Wukong contests scuttle with a clone bluff as often as with damage — the crab is won on the guess, not the duel.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Wukong if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Wukong takes objectives at a fair pace and can knock you out of the pit twice with a double-cast ultimate.","invade":"Walk into Wukong's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Wukong escapes an invade by leaving a clone behind, so commit your key ability only after the real one is confirmed.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. The clone walks in a straight line and does not react; the real Wukong is the one that changes direction.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Wukong's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Wukong is weakest with the clone spent, when he is a melee bruiser with one dash and no bluff left.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Wukong side lanes well and the clone makes a 1v1 answer into a coin flip you would rather not take.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Wukong picks are a Nimbus Strike into a double knock-up on a group, so spread before the spin rather than during.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Wukong wins by catching two or more people in the ultimate at the moment his team is ready to follow."},"Briar":{"tldr":"Briar adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Briar seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Even","why":"Both sides open with the same Blood Frenzy (W) auto-chase clear and the same execute-recast healing off missing-health targets. Neither Briar has a kit edge here — whoever times the recast cleaner and picks the healthier route gets there first, but that is a play-skill and pathing difference, not a matchup one."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Even","why":"Both Briars unlock the same Head Rush (Q) dash-stun at level 2. Whoever lands Q first wins the duel, since it strips armor and chains into the same auto-chasing Blood Frenzy on either side — this is a reflex and positioning matchup, not one the kit decides in advance."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Even","why":"Both sides now have Chilling Scream (E) to cancel a bad frenzy, charge damage reduction, or knock the other into terrain for a stun. Since the tool is identical on both sides of this duel, the fight comes down to who charges E first and who has spent more Fury, not anything the kit favors."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Briar's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Even","why":"Both sides get the same global Certain Death (R) mark-and-fear at level 6. Whichever Briar lands it first on the other's carry gets the map-wide dive; since the tool is mirrored, this is decided by who reads the map faster, not by anything the kit gives one side over the other."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Your clear runs itself, so you can sweep both sides before forcing highly aggressive neutral pit takes. This priority shatters their capacity to track your movements evenly."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"In the mirror both of you clear with Blood Frenzy healing and neither wins the early duel. The fight goes to whoever lands Head Rush (475 range, 13-second cooldown) first and whoever has more health when the frenzies meet, because missing health increases healing. Open where your strongest lane can help and frenzy through all six camps. Contest the scuttle only when you arrive with more health. Chilling Scream knocks her back into a wall if you charge it fully, so fight her near terrain. Recall at level 4. A ward on her raptors tells you which side she frenzies toward.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Briar is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Briar if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear.","invade":"Walk into Briar's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Briar's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing."},"Jax":{"tldr":"Jax adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Jax has no slow or kite tool — he stands and trades, using Counter Strike (E) to dodge and stun through your frenzy window and Empower (W) to punish your engage with a heavy burst auto, exploiting your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Jax attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Jax into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Jax's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Jax or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Jax's first item is a real threshold — the Empower-leap burst goes from a trade to a kill on squishier junglers."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Jax is even with you at level 1 because Counter Strike dodges your frenzy autos, but from level 2 your healing and Head Rush win. Frenzy through your camps and fight him for the scuttle at level 3. Counter Strike (17-second cooldown) dodges your attacks and stuns you at the end, so cancel Blood Frenzy with Chilling Scream when he spins, and come back after the stun. Leap Strike (700 range) is his only gap closer. Invade his raptors at level 3 if your lanes can follow, and ward his blue. Recall after the crab.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Jax is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Jax will take almost any scuttle contest, because the E stun turns a contested crab into a won duel.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Jax if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Jax is a slow objective taker early but a strong smite fighter, since the stun interrupts your attempt entirely.","invade":"Walk into Jax's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Invade Jax between camps rather than at one, since a camp beside him feeds Counter Strike just as your own attacks do.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Counter Strike has a two-second dodge window; the answer is to stop attacking and step out, not to trade through it.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Jax's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Jax is weakest with his E down and no camp beside him, which is the only version of this fight worth taking.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Jax is the best side laner in the jungle at full build and will take a 1v2 on that wave if you let him.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Jax does not pick people, he waits for one to walk into range, so respect his leap distance around walls.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Jax wins by getting to full build and holding a side lane that costs you two people to answer."},"Master Yi":{"tldr":"Master Yi adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Master Yi seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Master Yi attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Master Yi into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Master Yi's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Master Yi or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Master Yi's first item is the start of the curve rather than a spike — his real jump is the second and third."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Master Yi farms and does not want to fight you, and your frenzy beats him at every early level. Start on the side facing his first buff and invade at level 3 while he is still clearing. Alpha Strike (20-second cooldown) makes him untargetable, which breaks your frenzy lock, so Head Rush him right after he lands. Meditate heals him, but your stun interrupts it. He will not risk a scuttle fight, so take both crabs. Recall after taking his camps, and ward his blue so you can find him before his items arrive.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Master Yi is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Master Yi avoids scuttle contests before six — he takes the free crab and gives up the contested one.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Master Yi if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Master Yi has strong single-target objective damage but a weak pit fight, so contest his smites with crowd control.","invade":"Walk into Master Yi's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Master Yi is one of the best invade targets in the game before six, since Meditate only delays the outcome.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Alpha Strike makes him untargetable for its duration; hold your key ability for after it ends, not during.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Master Yi's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Master Yi is weakest from one to five, and everything he does later depends on how badly that window went.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Master Yi side lanes at full build and answering him alone there is a mistake, however far ahead you are.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Master Yi does not pick; he cleans up, so the danger is a fight your team half-loses rather than an ambush.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Master Yi wins by farming to full build and then resetting Highlander through a fight nobody can chain-stun."},"Olaf":{"tldr":"Olaf is a stand-and-fight duelist, not a kiter: Undertow (Q) grounds you, shutting off Head Rush and Blood Frenzy's dash for its duration if he plants an axe under you, and Ragnarok (R) makes him immune to your stuns, fear and knock-back while he's active, so timing your all-in around his ultimate matters more than usual. Briar answers with Head Rush (Q) to shred his armor and close in before the axe lands, then Blood Frenzy (W) to punish him once Ragnarok is down. Olaf scales off Berserker Rage and Reckless Swing's missing-health lifesteal and true damage, so a drawn-out fight favors him the lower his health drops -- do not let the duel go long against a healthy Olaf.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Olaf attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Olaf into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Olaf's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Olaf or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Olaf's first item is a large jump — the true damage plus lifesteal turns extended fights into ones he simply does not lose."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Olaf is the strongest early duelist in the game: he beats you badly at level 1 and is still ahead at levels 2 and 3. Ward both buffs before they spawn and start where your laners cover. Undertow (1000 range, 9-second cooldown) slows you, and Reckless Swing true damage out-damages your healing. Give up scuttle. If he never shows, finish your camps and go back at level 4. Never frenzy into him; Blood Frenzy will not let you leave once he starts winning. Fight only with a laner and after Tough It Out has been used.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Olaf is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Contest scuttle against Olaf only from full health, since his sustain and true damage beat most of the roster at that timer.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Olaf if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Olaf is a strong objective duellist because Reckless Swing ignores resistances and his health stays high through the fight.","invade":"Walk into Olaf's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Invade Olaf above half health and never inside his slow, because a low-health 1v1 in his own jungle is the fight he wants.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. The axe on the ground is the tell — an Olaf who cannot pick it back up has a long cooldown and no slow.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Olaf's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Olaf is weakest against distance: he has no gap-closer, so a wall between you and the axe line takes the fight away.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Olaf side lanes strongly and takes any 1v1 there, but he cannot answer a fight on the other side of the map.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Olaf does not pick; he runs people down, so the danger is a slow landing rather than an ambush.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Olaf wins by invading, snowballing early, and diving through crowd control before anyone can scale past him."},"Qiyana":{"tldr":"Qiyana adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Qiyana seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Qiyana attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Qiyana into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Qiyana's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Qiyana or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Qiyana's first item is the threshold where the element combo goes from a heavy trade to a full deletion."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Qiyana has no way to out-heal your bleed, and you win at levels 1 and 2 and by a lot at level 3. Full clear and invade her raptors at level 3. Terrashape (1100 range) is her dash and element pickup; wait for her to use it before you Head Rush. With the river element her Edge of Ixtal carries crowd control that interrupts a frenzy, so fight her away from water. Take the level-3 scuttle and recall after the invade, with a ward on the brush near your camps.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Qiyana is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Qiyana contests scuttle with the river element, where the slow makes the trade one-sided before it starts.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Qiyana if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Qiyana has poor objective damage and no way to hold a pit, so her smite fights are the weakest part of her game.","invade":"Walk into Qiyana's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Qiyana escapes an invade with Terrashape and Audacity, so cut the wall she is heading for rather than chasing.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Track which element she is holding — brush means stealth, river means slow, and rock means the wall stun is armed.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Qiyana's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Qiyana is weakest in open ground away from terrain, where the ultimate has nothing to stun against.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Qiyana side lanes to look for a solo kill rather than to push, and the wall-hop makes her hard to punish for it.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Qiyana picks are a brush-stealth Q onto someone alone, so sweep the bushes on the side she was last seen.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Qiyana wins by one-shotting a carry and using the wall stun to make the follow-up fight unwinnable."},"Shyvana":{"tldr":"Shyvana adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Shyvana seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, tank your frenzy behind Inferno Aegis (W) and Molten Burst (E) rather than kite it, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Shyvana attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Shyvana into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Shyvana's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Shyvana or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Shyvana's first item plus dragon form is the sharpest spike she gets — the farm bot becomes a duellist in one moment."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Shyvana has no hard crowd control before six and cannot stop a frenzy, so you beat her at every early level. Start on the side facing her first buff, clear two camps and invade at level 3. Inferno Aegis (13-second cooldown) gives her a shield and speed, so wait for it to end before you Head Rush. Molten Burst (800 range) slows you, but frenzy speed makes up for it. Take both scuttles so she collects fewer Scalemail stacks. Recall after taking her camps, and keep wards in her jungle.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Shyvana is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Shyvana takes scuttle quickly but has no crowd control to win a contested one before her ultimate.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Shyvana if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Shyvana is an excellent drake taker, so treat every early drake she has vision on as already contested.","invade":"Walk into Shyvana's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Shyvana is one of the best invade targets before six — no crowd control, no escape, and a clear she cannot abandon.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Watch her fury bar: a full bar means the transform is available and the fight she takes will be a different one.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Shyvana's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Shyvana is weakest before six, and her whole game is built on how much farm she banked during that window.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Shyvana side lanes extremely well at full build and is a genuine 1v1 threat to anyone who answers her alone.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Shyvana picks are a dragon-form flight into a knock-back, so keep out of the flight line when her ultimate is up.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Shyvana wins by farming untouched to two items and turning into a stat check most junglers cannot answer."},"Trundle":{"tldr":"Trundle adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Trundle seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Trundle attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Trundle into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Trundle's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Trundle or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Trundle's first item is a real threshold — the sustain plus stat theft makes long fights ones he cannot lose."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Trundle beats you at every early level, because Chomp (3.5-second cooldown) steals your AD with each bite and King's Tribute heals him through your bleed. Pillar of Ice (1000 range) also knocks you away from him mid-frenzy, which wastes your W. Ward both buffs before they spawn, start where your laners can cover, and give up the first scuttle. Full clear if he is not in your jungle and recall at level 4. Fight only when Pillar has been used and a laner is close, and open with a charged Chilling Scream rather than Blood Frenzy.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Trundle is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Contest scuttle against Trundle outside his Frozen Domain, because inside it the attack speed and stat steal decide the duel.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Trundle if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Trundle is an excellent objective duellist because Subjugate drains health and resistances at exactly the moment it matters.","invade":"Walk into Trundle's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Trundle invades and wins, so an invade against him only works with numbers or with him already low.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. The pillar is the tell — once it is placed your retreat line is gone, so move before it goes down and not after.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Trundle's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Trundle is weakest outside his Frozen Domain, where the attack speed bonus does not apply and his damage is ordinary.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Trundle side lanes very well and takes towers fast, and answering him alone in his own zone rarely works.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Trundle picks are a pillar behind you at a choke, so cross corridors with a dash available or not at all.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Trundle wins by taking every duel and every objective and stealing the stats that would have answered him."},"Udyr":{"tldr":"Udyr adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Udyr seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Udyr attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Udyr into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Udyr's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) gives you a long-range global initiation and a fear on arrival, but it grants no unstoppable or CC-immune state — Udyr's Blazing Stampede (E) stun and Wingborne Storm (R) slow can still interrupt your approach or punish the dive. Time the cast from fog of war so you land on an isolated target, and expect to fight through his kit rather than through it unimpeded. This is your biggest mechanical spike, turning you into a real cross-map threat, but it is not an unstoppable one."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Udyr's first item is where the awakened stance rotations stop being a heavy trade and start being a kill."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Udyr clears extremely fast and his stance swaps give him a stun and a shield on short cooldowns, so he wins every early fight against you. Blazing Stampede stuns you when he arrives and comes back 6 seconds after a swap, and Iron Mantle shields him while your bleed ticks. Ward both buffs, start where your laners cover and let him have scuttle. Full clear only if he has been seen elsewhere, and recall at level 4. Your Head Rush is best used after his stun has gone onto a laner, with that laner still standing next to you.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Udyr is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Contest scuttle against Udyr before he has two stance points, because the awakened trade pattern beats most kits at level three.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Udyr if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Udyr is a strong objective duellist with high sustained damage but no way to zone you out of the pit.","invade":"Walk into Udyr's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Udyr wins most invades fought straight, so the answer is to take his camps while he is on the far side.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Blazing Stampede only travels in a straight line, so breaking the line with terrain removes the stun entirely.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Udyr's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Udyr is weakest against distance and walls, since he has no ranged threat and no way to catch a champion who leaves.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Udyr side lanes strongly and takes towers quickly, but he cannot answer a fight happening anywhere else.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Udyr does not pick; he runs you down, so the danger is being caught in a corridor rather than being ambushed.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Udyr wins by taking every fight he can reach and every objective he can stand next to before the carries scale."},"Vi":{"tldr":"Vi adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Vi seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Vi attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Vi into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Vi's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) gives you a long-range global initiation and a fear on arrival, but it does not make you unstoppable or CC-immune — Vi's Cease and Desist (R) grounds your dashes outright and can hard-CC you the moment you land. Time the cast from fog of war onto an isolated target and expect her ult to answer yours if she has it up. This is your biggest mechanical spike and turns you into a real map-wide threat, just not an untouchable one."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Vi's first item is where the charge-and-shred pattern stops being a chunk and starts closing out squishier junglers."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Vi clears steadily and ganks with Vault Breaker, but your frenzy healing beats her at every early level. Full clear and meet her at scuttle. Vault Breaker (12-second cooldown) knocks you back and breaks your frenzy lock, so Head Rush her first to stop the charge. Denting Blows shreds your armor over time, so finish the fight rather than trading back and forth. Invade her raptors at level 3 when she has been seen at a lane. Recall after the crab, and ward her blue to see her next route.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Vi is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Vi contests scuttle with a charged Vault Breaker, which wins the crab by moving you off it as much as by damage.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Vi if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Vi has good objective damage from the armour shred but cannot hold a pit once her charge is spent.","invade":"Walk into Vi's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Vi escapes an invade with the same charge she engages with, so the punish window is right after that Q lands.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. The charge-up is visible and slow — step behind a camp while it winds and the whole engage is wasted.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Vi's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Vi is weakest with her Q on cooldown, when she is a melee champion with no gap-closer and no escape.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Vi side lanes adequately but would rather be near her team, where a point-and-click lockdown starts a fight.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Vi picks are Cease and Desist on whoever she can reach, and it cannot be dodged, so respect the health threshold.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Vi wins by locking down the one target her team needs removed and shredding the armour off it."},"Xin Zhao":{"tldr":"Xin Zhao adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Xin Zhao seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Xin Zhao attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Xin Zhao into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Xin Zhao's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) gives you a long-range global initiation and a fear on arrival, but it does not make you unstoppable — Xin Zhao's Crescent Guard (R) knocks you back and makes him impervious to your damage from outside its ring the instant you land on him. Time the cast from fog of war onto an isolated target and treat this as your biggest mechanical spike, not a guaranteed kill through his ultimate."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Xin Zhao's first item is a sharp jump — the knock-up combo goes from a strong trade to a kill on most junglers."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Xin Zhao is ahead of you at levels 1 and 2 and even at level 3. Audacious Charge (650 range, 11-second cooldown) closes on you, and his Three Talon Strike knock-up interrupts your frenzy. He likes to walk into the buff on his side, so ward it and start where your lanes can help. Skip any scuttle fight before level 3. By level 3, a charged Chilling Scream stuns him against a wall, so fight near terrain. Recall after the full clear and take a fight only after his knock-up has been used.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Xin Zhao is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Contest scuttle against Xin Zhao only with a health lead — the challenge poke into the knock-up is one of the best level-three duels.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Xin Zhao if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Xin Zhao is a strong objective duellist and Crescent Guard can remove everyone but you from the pit fight.","invade":"Walk into Xin Zhao's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Xin Zhao wins invades fought straight, so the answer is to take his camps rather than to meet him at one.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. The third Q hit is the knock-up — disengage after the second, and the combo has nothing left to chain.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Xin Zhao's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Xin Zhao is weakest against ranged kiting once his charge is spent, since he has nothing else that closes a gap.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Xin Zhao side lanes well early but falls behind the real side laners once full builds arrive.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Xin Zhao picks are an Audacious Charge from a bush into the knock-up, so respect river bushes on his side.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Xin Zhao wins by snowballing the early game and using Crescent Guard to make one late fight a 1v1 he chose."},"Amumu":{"tldr":"Amumu adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Amumu seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Amumu attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Amumu into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Amumu's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Amumu or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Amumu's first completed item makes Despair and Tantrum clear at real speed and turns his engage into a genuine team-fight threat."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Amumu full clears safely but loses a duel to you at every early level. Start on the side facing his first buff, clear two camps and invade at level 3. Bandage Toss (1100 range) is his only engage, so walk out of its line before you Head Rush. Tantrum reduces your physical damage and comes back faster every time you hit him, so pop Chilling Scream and heal while he waits. Despair drains your health in a long fight, but your bleed heals more. Take the crabs he cannot contest and recall once his raptors are dead.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Amumu is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Amumu contests scuttle with the Bandage Toss, not with damage — if the bandage misses he loses the crab and the trade.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Amumu if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Amumu is a fast grub and drake taker because Despair burns percent health, but he needs a body between him and your smite.","invade":"Walk into Amumu's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Amumu has no dash and no escape, so an invade that starts outside bandage range is close to free.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Watch the Bandage Toss cooldown — with it down Amumu is a slow melee champion with no way to start anything.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Amumu's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Amumu is weakest between one and five, when his own duel is nothing and his ganks still need a laner to hold the target.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Amumu cannot hold a side lane; leaving him alone on a wave concedes almost nothing.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Amumu picks come from fog bandages at river entrances, so hug the wall he cannot line up against.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Amumu wins by landing one Curse of the Sad Mummy on two or more people and letting his team clean up."},"Hecarim":{"tldr":"Hecarim adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Hecarim isn't a kiter — Devastating Charge (E) lets him run through units and close distance faster than you can frenzy away, so he looks to chase you down and trade through his Spirit of Dread (W) sustain, exploiting your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Hecarim attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Hecarim into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Hecarim's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Hecarim or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Hecarim's first item is where the Rampage spam stops being clear speed and starts being a real health bar of damage."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Hecarim clears very fast with Rampage and often runs to a lane at level 3, but you win the duel at levels 1 and 2 and by a wide margin at 3. Full clear and take the camps on the side he just left. If he comes to you, Head Rush him before Devastating Charge (20-second cooldown) builds up speed. Spirit of Dread heals him off nearby damage, but your bleed heals more. Invade his raptors at level 3 when your lanes are pushed. Recall after the invade, and ward his blue to track his route. Take the scuttle on his side once he has charged into a lane.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Hecarim is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Hecarim wins scuttle fights by arriving with speed already built, so the crab is usually decided before you see him.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Hecarim if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Hecarim takes objectives quickly off Rampage stacks and can disengage a lost smite fight faster than most.","invade":"Walk into Hecarim's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Hecarim is hard to catch in an invade — the passive speed and Devastating Charge mean he leaves whenever he chooses.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Watch how fast he is moving: a Hecarim already at speed is committed to a charge, and the knock-back is coming.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Hecarim's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Hecarim is weakest in a confined space with no runway, where Devastating Charge cannot build to anything.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Hecarim side lanes to build a lead and rotates faster than anyone answering him, so the wave is never the whole story.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Hecarim picks are a long charge out of fog into a knock-back against a wall, so keep open ground behind you.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Hecarim wins by reaching your back line before the fight has shape, usually through an Onslaught of Shadows fear."},"Jarvan IV":{"tldr":"Jarvan IV adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Jarvan IV isn't a kiter — he all-ins with Dragon Strike (Q) into Demacian Standard (E) for a knockup, backed by Golden Aegis's (W) shield and slow, and can trap you in a Cataclysm (R) arena, exploiting your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Jarvan IV attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Jarvan IV into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Jarvan IV's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Jarvan IV or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Jarvan IV's first item makes the flag-drag rotation a genuine kill threat rather than a set-up for someone else."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Jarvan IV spends his early game ganking with his flag, and in the jungle your frenzy healing out-lasts him. Clear all six camps and fight him over the scuttle. Demacian Standard (860 range) into Dragon Strike knocks you up, so walk out of the line between him and the flag before you Head Rush. Golden Aegis (9-second cooldown) soaks your first burst, so save Head Rush until the shield has broken. When he uses flag and Q to gank a lane, take his camps on the other side. Recall after that invade.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Jarvan IV is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Jarvan IV contests scuttle with the E-Q knock-up, which wins the crab and the trade if you are standing on it.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Jarvan IV if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Jarvan IV takes objectives at a fair pace and can wall off the pit with Cataclysm so the smite fight never happens.","invade":"Walk into Jarvan IV's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Jarvan IV can flag out of most invades, so the punish window is right after that flag has been spent.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. The flag is the tell — once it is on the ground the knock-up is coming, so move off the line rather than back.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Jarvan IV's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Jarvan IV is weakest once the flag is on cooldown, when he has no engage, no escape and modest damage.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Jarvan IV holds a side lane adequately but would rather be near an objective his cage can decide.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Jarvan IV picks are a flag-drag onto someone crossing a choke, so cross with a dash available or not at all.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Jarvan IV wins by caging the person who matters at the start of a fight and letting his team collapse on it."},"Maokai":{"tldr":"Maokai adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Maokai seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Maokai attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Maokai into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Maokai's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Maokai or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Maokai's first item mostly buys health and cooldowns — his spike is durability, not damage, and it arrives early."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Maokai clears slowly for his damage and loses to you at every early level. Start near his side and walk in at level 3 while his saplings are still going into camps. Twisted Advance (525 range, 14-second cooldown) roots you and makes him untargetable while he travels, which stops your frenzy, so wait for it before you commit. Sapling Toss hides saplings in brush, and Blood Frenzy will chase you into them, so ward before you walk in. Scuttle is yours whenever he is not already standing on it with a sapling. Recall after taking his camps, and ward his blue for the next invade.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Maokai is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Maokai contests scuttle with roots rather than damage — the crab goes to whoever he can hold in place.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Maokai if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Maokai is a slow objective taker but an excellent pit defender, since Nature's Grasp arrives before the fight does.","invade":"Walk into Maokai's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Maokai survives most invades on sustain alone, so an invade only pays if it takes the camp rather than the kill.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Twisted Advance is the engage; while he is untargetable in it the root is already decided, so pre-move instead.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Maokai's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Maokai is weakest as a damage threat — he can hold you but rarely kills you without a laner arriving.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Maokai does not side lane meaningfully; his value is holding the river and the pits for his team.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Maokai picks are a sapling into a root at a choke, so break line of sight rather than walking the bush line.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Maokai wins by making the river his zone and starting every objective fight with a wall of roots."},"Nunu & Willump":{"tldr":"Nunu & Willump isn't a kiter, he's a control mage who wants to lock you down: Snowball Barrage (E) roots if the snowballs connect, Biggest Snowball Ever! (W) can knock you up from way out in the map, and Absolute Zero (R) is a channeled blizzard that punishes you for frenzying in on top of it. Briar answers with Head Rush (Q) to shred his armor and close the distance before the snowball grows, then Blood Frenzy (W) to run him down once he's exposed. Nunu scales toward a big-ultimate teamfight threat and off Consume (Q) true-damage sustain in his own clear; he does not out-race you early, so the matchup is decided by whether you can reach him before Absolute Zero finishes charging.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Nunu & Willump attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Nunu & Willump into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Nunu & Willump's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Nunu & Willump or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Nunu & Willump's first item mostly buys durability and cooldowns, so his spike is objective control rather than damage."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Nunu & Willump clear fast with Consume, and Consume wins every smite race, but in a fight your frenzy beats him at every early level. Clear toward his side, and at level 3 frenzy into his camps as soon as the snowball rolls toward a lane. Kill the scuttle before it drops low, because Consume (13-second cooldown) steals it. Snowball Barrage roots anyone its snowballs touched when he stops throwing, which ends your frenzy, so Head Rush him the moment he starts. Head home once his camps are yours.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Nunu & Willump is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Nunu & Willump does not win a scuttle duel, but Consume cheats the crab out from under you in a race.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Nunu & Willump if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Nunu & Willump is the best objective thief in the game — never let a pit reach smite range with him nearby.","invade":"Walk into Nunu & Willump's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Nunu & Willump loses almost any invade fought honestly, since the kit is gank pressure rather than duel pressure.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. The snowball is the tell — a rolling Nunu is committed, and stepping out of the line takes the knock-up away.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Nunu & Willump's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Nunu & Willump is weakest in a straight 1v1 at every stage of the game, which is why he never wants one.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Nunu & Willump does not side lane; he shadows objectives and waits for a smite fight he can cheat.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Nunu & Willump picks come from a long snowball out of fog, so cross river where the roll cannot build.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Nunu & Willump wins by stealing objectives and channelling Absolute Zero into a fight nobody can leave."},"Rammus":{"tldr":"Rammus doesn't kite you, he tanks the frenzy: Defensive Ball Curl (W) spikes his Armor/MR and reflects damage back at you, which cuts into both the damage and the bleed-heal Blood Frenzy relies on, and Frenzying Taunt (E) locks you onto him specifically, which can waste your automated pursuit on a target built to punish auto-attacking him. Briar answers with Head Rush (Q) to shred that Armor before he curls up, and needs to land it early in the trade rather than after Rammus already has Defensive Ball Curl active. Rammus wants to Powerball (Q) in, taunt, and soak while his team collapses; watch for that gank pattern rather than a straight duel.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Rammus attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Rammus into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Rammus's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Rammus or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Rammus' first item is an armour spike more than a damage one, which is exactly what makes him harder to fight."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Rammus is the one tank that hurts you for frenzying: Defensive Ball Curl reflects your attacks, and Frenzying Taunt forces you to keep swinging into it. You still win the early fight, but only if you respect W. Full clear, and take the scuttle before he rolls there. When he curls (7-second cooldown), stop attacking and use Chilling Scream to heal while the curl runs out, then Head Rush him. Powerball is his only engage. Invade his raptors at level 3 when he has rolled away to gank, and recall after the invade.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Rammus is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Rammus contests scuttle by rolling in and taunting — the crab is decided by whether you can leave, not by damage.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Rammus if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Rammus takes objectives slowly but defends a pit well, since a taunt at smite range ends the contest.","invade":"Walk into Rammus's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Rammus is a bad invade target for any auto-attack champion, because the reflect turns your damage back on you.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. While the ball is curled, stop attacking — every auto you throw into it is damage you take instead.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Rammus's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Rammus is weakest against ability damage and against anything that does not need to auto-attack him at all.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Rammus does not side lane; he rolls between objectives and lanes where the taunt has follow-up.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Rammus picks are a Powerball out of fog into a taunt, so watch for the roll starting long before it reaches you.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Rammus wins by locking down the person your team most needs held and surviving everything sent at him."},"Rek'Sai":{"tldr":"Rek'Sai isn't a kiter, she's an ambush fighter: Burrow (W) grounds you, shutting off Head Rush/Blood Frenzy's dash if she catches you while burrowed, and Void Rush (R) is a percent-max-health execute that goes untargetable on the way in, punishing you for stacking raw HP instead of resistances. Briar answers with Head Rush (Q) to shred her armor before she can Un-burrow safely, and Chilling Scream (E) to knock her off a Furious Bite true-damage all-in. Rek'Sai wants to tunnel around the map for surprise counter-ganks and objective steals rather than out-race your clear, so track her tunnels and Burrow timer rather than expecting a straight kite.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Rek'Sai attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Rek'Sai into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Rek'Sai's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Rek'Sai or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Rek'Sai's first item is a real jump in duel power, but it is also close to the end of her scaling curve."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Rek'Sai beats you at level 1 with Queen's Wrath, is even at level 2, and at level 3 your frenzy healing wins. Frenzy through the camps on the side away from her opening buff. Un-burrow (4-second cooldown) knocks you up out of your frenzy, so wait for her to surface before you Head Rush. Tunnel lets her escape faster than you can chase, so ward her exits near your camps. Take the level-3 scuttle, and recall after that fight.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Rek'Sai is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Rek'Sai wins scuttle contests off an Unburrow knock-up, which lands from a direction the crab fight does not expect.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Rek'Sai if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Rek'Sai is a strong objective duellist because Furious Bite is true damage and Void Rush executes the contest.","invade":"Walk into Rek'Sai's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Rek'Sai invades through her own tunnel network, so the entrances she has dug are the map you actually need warded.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Burrowed Rek'Sai shows tremors, not a champion — if she is burrowed near you the knock-up is already in range.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Rek'Sai's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Rek'Sai is weakest late, when the early tunnel pressure stops mattering and her damage falls behind the carries.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Rek'Sai side lanes to keep tunnel pressure rather than to push, so the wave is rarely why she is there.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Rek'Sai picks are an Unburrow from an unwarded tunnel, so sweep the exits rather than the bushes.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Rek'Sai wins by converting an early tunnel-tempo lead into objectives before her scaling runs out."},"Sejuani":{"tldr":"Sejuani adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Sejuani seeks to out-scale your kit into a frontline teamfight tank, lock you down with Frost stacks into Permafrost (E) and a global Glacial Prison (R) stun rather than kite, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Sejuani attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Sejuani into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Sejuani's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Sejuani or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Sejuani's first item is a durability spike — she does not start killing you, she starts being impossible to remove."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Sejuani needs allies to stack Permafrost, so alone in her jungle she loses to your frenzy at every early level. Clear toward her jungle and frenzy into her at level 3, while Winter's Wrath is still spent on camps. Arctic Assault (650 range, 18-second cooldown) is her only engage; once it is used, she cannot get away from Blood Frenzy. Her tank stats slow the kill, so pop Chilling Scream mid-fight to top up. Both crabs are yours; recall when her camps are gone.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Sejuani is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Sejuani contests scuttle with Permafrost stuns rather than damage — she wins the crab when a laner is with her.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Sejuani if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Sejuani takes objectives slowly but holds a pit very well, since Glacial Prison starts the fight on her terms.","invade":"Walk into Sejuani's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Sejuani survives an invade far better than she wins one; expect her to walk out rather than die in it.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Her passive frost armour is the tell — a Sejuani who has not taken damage recently is much harder to burst.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Sejuani's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Sejuani is weakest as a solo damage threat, since almost everything she does needs a teammate to finish.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Sejuani does not side lane; she plays the river and the pits, where a cross-map stun is worth more than a wave.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Sejuani picks are a long Glacial Prison from fog, so keep terrain between you and the direction she disappeared.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Sejuani wins by landing one cross-map stun into a fight her team is already positioned for."},"Skarner":{"tldr":"Skarner adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Skarner seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Skarner attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Skarner into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Skarner's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Skarner or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Skarner's first item buys the health and cooldowns that let him survive the answer to his own engage."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Skarner ganks through terrain with Ixtal's Impact, but you win at levels 1 and 2 and by a lot at 3. Full clear and fight him at scuttle out in the open, away from walls. Ixtal's Impact (1700 range, 22-second cooldown) stuns you if he pins you on a wall, and Blood Frenzy can chase you straight into one, so Head Rush him before the charge. Seismic Bastion shields him, but your bleed heals through it. Invade his raptors at level 3 once he has used the charge on a lane. Recall after the invade.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Skarner is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Skarner contests scuttle with the wall stun — near terrain the crab fight is his, and in the open it is not.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Skarner if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Skarner holds a pit well because Impale removes whoever steps up to contest the smite.","invade":"Walk into Skarner's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Skarner is durable enough to survive an invade but slow enough that he cannot punish one that leaves.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Terrain is the tell — Skarner near a wall has a stun, and Skarner in the open river has a slow and nothing else.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Skarner's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Skarner is weakest in open ground, where Ixtal's Impact cannot connect anyone to a wall.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Skarner does not side lane; he plays the pits, where a suppression on the right target decides the objective.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Skarner picks are an Impale on whoever walks a corridor first, so never lead a rotation through a choke.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Skarner wins by dragging one key target into his team at the start of every objective fight."},"Volibear":{"tldr":"Volibear adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Volibear seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Volibear attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Volibear into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Volibear's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) gives you a long-range global initiation and a fear on arrival, but it grants no CC-immunity — Volibear's Thundering Smash (Q) stun still lands on you the instant you arrive, and Stormbringer (R) can turn a dive back on you if he has it up. Time the cast from fog of war onto an isolated target and expect his Q to answer your landing. This is your biggest mechanical spike and turns you into a real map-wide threat, not an untouchable one."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Volibear's first item is where the bite trades stop being even and start ending with your health bar gone."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Volibear beats you at level 1 because Frenzied Maul bites harder than your bleed heals, is even at level 2, and at level 3 your healing and Head Rush pull ahead. Start as far from his opening buff as your leash allows and full clear. Thundering Smash (12-second cooldown) stuns you mid-frenzy, so wait for him to use it before you commit. Sky Splitter (1200 range) only shields him if he lands inside it, so drag the frenzy away from the circle. Take the level-3 scuttle and recall after the crab. Ward his raptors, because he walks in at level 1.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Volibear is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Volibear takes most scuttle contests — the stun into the maul bite pattern is one of the better level-three duels.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Volibear if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Volibear is a strong objective duellist and can disable a tower afterwards, so a won pit fight costs you twice.","invade":"Walk into Volibear's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Volibear wins most invades fought straight, and the Q stun means walking away from him is not simple.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Thundering Smash has to run at you in a straight line, so a wall or a camp between you removes the stun.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Volibear's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Volibear is weakest against ranged kiting, since he has no way to close a gap before six.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Volibear side lanes strongly and takes towers fast, which makes ignoring the wave expensive.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Volibear picks are a Stormbringer leap onto a group, so spread off the landing marker rather than running from it.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Volibear wins by brawling through the mid game and using the ultimate to take towers and objectives on the same trip."},"Warwick":{"tldr":"Warwick adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Warwick seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Warwick attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Warwick into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Warwick's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) gives you a long-range global initiation and a fear on arrival, but it grants no CC-immunity — Warwick's Infinite Duress (R) is a global suppress of its own, and if he lands it on you mid-dive you're locked down with no answer. Time your cast so you're not diving into an active Infinite Duress threat, and treat this as your biggest mechanical spike rather than an untouchable one."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Warwick's first item is where the healing stops being sustain and starts being more than your damage can out-pace."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Warwick is ahead of you at levels 1 and 2 and even at 3, because his healing matches yours and Blood Hunt (4000 range) finds you when you are low. Ward both buffs, start where your laners cover, and give up the scuttle before level 3. Jaws of the Beast (8-second cooldown) follows your dashes, so Head Rush will not get you away from it. Primal Howl fears you and ends your frenzy. Recall after the full clear, and fight him at level 3 only after Primal Howl has been used.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Warwick is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Contest scuttle against Warwick from full health, since his sustain out-lasts what most junglers can put out at that timer.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Warwick if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Warwick is a strong objective duellist with the Q percent-health damage and can hold the pit through a long fight.","invade":"Walk into Warwick's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Invade Warwick above fifty percent health, since below it his sustain and Blood Hunt win the fight your invade was meant to end.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Blood Hunt tracks anyone below half; if your health drops he gets speed toward you and you will not out-run it.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Warwick's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Warwick is weakest above fifty percent health, where the tracking does not apply and his damage is much lower.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Warwick side lanes adequately but his real value is answering any low-health fight anywhere on the map.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Warwick picks are an Infinite Duress onto whoever is lowest, so recall earlier than feels necessary against him.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Warwick wins by suppressing a carry for the length of a fight while out-healing everything sent back at him."},"Zac":{"tldr":"Zac adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Zac seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Zac attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Zac into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Zac's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) gives you a long-range global initiation and a fear on arrival, but it grants no CC-immunity — Zac's Elastic Slingshot (E) grounds your dashes outright, and Let's Bounce! (R) can knock you up repeatedly the moment he turns to fight. Time the cast from fog of war onto an isolated target and treat this as your biggest mechanical spike, not a guaranteed kill through his own CC."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Zac's first item is a durability spike, so he does not start killing you — he starts surviving whatever you send."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Zac's healing comes from blobs, and your bleed heals more, so you win at every early level. Start toward his side and invade at level 3 while his blobs are scattered around his camps. Elastic Slingshot (21-second cooldown) knocks you up out of your frenzy, but the long charge gives you time to Head Rush him before he launches. Frenzy through his blobs so he cannot pick them back up. Stretching Strikes (800 range) can grab you out of a frenzy, so Head Rush in from outside its reach. Take scuttle whenever he has used E to gank, and recall after the invade.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Zac is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Zac contests scuttle with a Slingshot from fog rather than a duel — the crab goes to whoever gets knocked up.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Zac if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Zac takes objectives slowly but survives a pit fight better than most, and the passive blob buys a second attempt.","invade":"Walk into Zac's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Zac loses a straight invade but is hard to kill in one, so an invade against him usually costs more time than it earns.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. The Slingshot charge is visible from far away — ward the walls he charges from and the engage never lands.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Zac's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Zac is weakest when his E is on cooldown and his passive blob has already been used, which is a long window.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Zac does not side lane; he lurks near objectives where a fog engage is worth more than a wave.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Zac picks are a long-range Slingshot into a group, so hold a dash for the landing rather than for the follow-up.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Zac wins by starting objective fights from fog with his whole team behind him and two health bars in front."},"Brand":{"tldr":"Brand adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Brand seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Brand attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Brand into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Brand's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Brand or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Brand's first item makes the Sear-into-Conflagration rotation a full health bar on a squishy, with no auto-attacks needed."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Brand burns you from range, but he has no dash and cannot stop a Head Rush, so you beat him at levels 1 and 2 and by a wide margin at 3. Start on the side facing his first buff and invade at level 2, while he is still spending mana on camps. Sear (1050 range, 8-second cooldown) stuns you only if you are ablaze, so Head Rush in before Conflagration lands on you. Pillar of Flame hits hard, but Chilling Scream heals you through it. Take both scuttles and recall after the invade, when he is out of mana.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Brand is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Brand wins a scuttle contest at range rather than at the crab — he will chip you off it instead of fighting for it.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Brand if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Brand melts objectives with the Blaze percent-health burn, so treat any pit he has vision on as contested.","invade":"Walk into Brand's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Brand has no dash at all, so an invade that arrives from two directions ends with him dead in his own jungle.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Watch his mana and the Sear cooldown — a Brand without the stun cannot start anything on you.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Brand's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Brand is weakest when Sear is on cooldown and there is only one target near him for Conflagration to bounce from.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Brand does not hold a side lane; he shoves it and leaves, so answer the wave and not the champion.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Brand picks are a Sear from fog into the full rotation, so break line of sight at the entrances he likes.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Brand wins by dragging fights next to his laners where Pyroclasm can bounce, and by burning objectives faster than you can."},"Fiddlesticks":{"tldr":"Fiddlesticks adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Fiddlesticks seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Fiddlesticks attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Fiddlesticks into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Fiddlesticks's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Fiddlesticks or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Fiddlesticks' first item turns the drain and the fear into a real health bar of damage rather than a delay."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Fiddlesticks is weak early and cannot survive a frenzy, so you beat him at every level. Start on the side facing his first buff and invade at level 3 from a side his A Harmless Scarecrow effigies do not watch. Terrify (575 range, 15-second cooldown) fears you and cancels your frenzy, so Head Rush in only after he has used it on a camp. Bountiful Harvest drains you, but your bleed heals more than it takes. Kill the effigies you find, take both scuttles, and recall once his camps are gone.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Fiddlesticks is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Fiddlesticks avoids a straight scuttle contest before six and would rather bluff you off the crab with an effigy.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Fiddlesticks if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Fiddlesticks drains objectives quickly, but the channel means any interruption costs him the whole attempt.","invade":"Walk into Fiddlesticks's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Fiddlesticks is very weak to an early invade — he has no mobility and the drain is cancelled by any damage.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. The effigies are free information: a fake Fiddlesticks in your jungle usually means the real one is somewhere else.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Fiddlesticks's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Fiddlesticks is weakest before six, when Terrify is his only real answer and his clear has left him low.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Fiddlesticks does not side lane; he sits in fog near an objective and waits for the fight to come to him.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Fiddlesticks picks are a Crowstorm out of unwarded fog, so deep wards are worth more than any item against him.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Fiddlesticks wins by landing one unseen ultimate into a grouped fight, which is why vision is the entire counter-play."},"Gragas":{"tldr":"Gragas adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Gragas has no mobility besides his short-range Body Slam (E) engage, so instead of kiting he looks to land that stun and burst you down with Barrel Roll (Q) and Drunken Rage (W) before you can lock onto him, exploiting your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Gragas attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Gragas into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Gragas's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Gragas or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Gragas' first item makes the Barrel Roll into Body Slam combo a real chunk instead of a nuisance, on a short cooldown."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Gragas heals with Happy Hour and can bump you out of a frenzy, but you still beat him at levels 1 and 2 and by a wide margin at 3. Full clear and meet him at scuttle away from walls, so Body Slam cannot bump you into terrain. Body Slam (600 range, 14-second cooldown) knocks you back and stuns, so Head Rush him before he can line it up. Drunken Rage reduces the damage he takes, so pop Chilling Scream and heal while it runs out. Invade his raptors at level 3 once he has used Body Slam on a lane, and recall after the invade.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Gragas is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Gragas contests scuttle with the Body Slam knock-back — he does not need to win the fight, only to move you off it.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Gragas if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Gragas is an awkward objective fighter alone, but with Explosive Cask he can simply remove you from the pit.","invade":"Walk into Gragas's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Gragas escapes an invade with Body Slam through a wall, so the punish window is the seconds after that E lands.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Watch the Body Slam cooldown — it is his engage and his escape, and he cannot have both at once.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Gragas's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Gragas is weakest with his E down, since his damage without the slam engage is poke and nothing else.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Gragas shoves a side lane with Barrel Roll and rotates rather than duelling, so he is often two waves from the fight.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Gragas picks are a Cask from over a wall that separates one person from the group at a choke.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Gragas wins by displacing whoever matters most at the moment the fight starts, usually around an objective pit."},"Ivern":{"tldr":"Ivern adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Ivern's Friend of the Forest passive means he can't fight or take camps head-on at all, so he isn't racing your clear — he's using Rootcaller (Q) to root you from 1125 range and enable his laner or Daisy, and Triggerseed (E) to shield/slow if you catch him, exploiting your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Ivern attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Ivern into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Ivern's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Ivern or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Ivern's first item mostly buys shield strength and cooldowns — his spike is what his carry does, not what he does."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Ivern cannot kill camps quickly and cannot fight you at all early, so you win at every level. He marks a camp and waits beside it for the camp to be freed, which is exactly when you should Head Rush him. Start on the side facing his first buff and walk in at level 3. Rootcaller (1125 range, 14-second cooldown) is his only crowd control, so step out of its line before you commit. Brushmaker hides him in new brush, so ward before you frenzy. Take both scuttles and recall after stealing his marked camps.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Ivern is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Ivern does not contest scuttle on his own; if he shows at the crab, a laner is already in the river with him.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Ivern if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Ivern takes objectives with a free smite and Daisy as the body, so treat a pit he has vision on as a two-body fight.","invade":"Walk into Ivern's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Ivern loses any invade he is caught alone in — the kit is a root and a shield, with nothing that trades back.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Watch the marked camps: a freed camp on your side of the map means Ivern has already been there and left.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Ivern's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Ivern is weakest in any straight 1v1, at every level, which is why he never takes one voluntarily.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Ivern does not hold a side lane; he shields whoever does and makes that lane a 2v1 you have to answer with numbers.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Ivern picks are a Rootcaller onto a target his team can reach, so stay outside root range of his brush.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Ivern wins by making his carry unkillable and his jungle free, which is a tempo lead rather than a fighting one."},"Karthus":{"tldr":"Karthus adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Karthus seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Karthus attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Karthus into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Karthus's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Karthus or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Karthus' first item is where Lay Waste stops chipping and starts taking a third of a health bar per cast."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Karthus has the fastest clear in the game, but he is squishy and slow, so one frenzy kills him at any early level. Start on the side facing his first buff and invade at level 3 while he stands still casting Lay Waste. Wall of Pain (15-second cooldown) slows you as you cross it, so Head Rush over it rather than walking through. Death Defied lets him keep casting after he dies, so step away from his body once he falls. Take both scuttles and recall before Requiem is available at level 6.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Karthus is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Karthus rarely contests a scuttle directly — he takes the free one and out-farms you for the one he skipped.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Karthus if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Karthus melts objectives with Defile, so a pit he reaches first is usually gone before you arrive.","invade":"Walk into Karthus's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Karthus is very weak to an early invade, but Death Defied means killing him still costs you the following seconds.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Watch Wall of Pain: once it is placed he is committed to the fight, and before that he is only farming.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Karthus's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Karthus is weakest at melee range, where the isolated Lay Waste bonus does not apply and he cannot walk away.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Karthus shoves side waves faster than anyone but has no answer to a champion who arrives while he is doing it.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Karthus does not pick; he finishes, so the danger is the recall you take at low health rather than the fight.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Karthus wins by out-farming the map and cashing that lead into Requiem finishes on fights he was never in."},"Lillia":{"tldr":"Lillia adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Lillia seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Lillia attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Lillia into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Lillia's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Lillia or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Lillia's first item is when the passing damage becomes real — she stops chipping and starts out-pacing health bars."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Lillia kites everything with her passive speed, but Blood Frenzy gives you speed of your own and Head Rush closes the last gap, so you win at every early level. Start on the side facing her first buff and walk into her raptors at level 3, where she has to stand near the camp. Watch Out! Eep! (14-second cooldown) deals its big damage in the center, so frenzy onto her from the edge after she has cast it. Swirlseed slows you from far away, so dodge it before you commit. Take both scuttles, and recall once she has lost a camp or her flash.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Lillia is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Lillia contests scuttle by out-running you to it rather than by fighting, and leaves the moment you commit.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Lillia if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Lillia has good objective damage but a poor pit fight, so contest her smite attempts with a body rather than a race.","invade":"Walk into Lillia's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Lillia is hard to invade because the passive movement speed means she is gone before the second person arrives.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Swirlseed is her commitment: once the seed lands she will fight, and before that she is only kiting.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Lillia's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Lillia is weakest against anything that can close the gap on her, since her damage is over time and not burst.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Lillia side lanes fast and disengages faster, so answering her alone with a slow champion accomplishes nothing.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Lillia picks come from a rolled Swirlseed down a corridor, so cross river in the open rather than through a lane.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Lillia wins by kiting until her dream-dust damage adds up and using the sleep to make one fight unfair."},"Morgana":{"tldr":"Morgana adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Morgana seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Morgana attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Morgana into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Morgana's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Morgana or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Morgana's first item makes the binding-into-zone rotation a real chunk instead of a set-up for somebody else."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Morgana clears very fast with Tormented Shadow, but she has no escape and dies to a frenzy at every early level. Start on the side facing her first buff and invade at level 3 while she stands in her own pool. Dark Binding (1250 range, 10-second cooldown) roots you and ends your chase, so walk sideways when she aims it and Head Rush in after it misses. Black Shield blocks your stun, so wait for her to put it on herself first. She cannot hold a scuttle against you, so take both and recall after stealing her raptors.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Morgana is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Morgana contests scuttle with a Dark Binding rather than a duel — the crab is lost to the root, not to the damage.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Morgana if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Morgana takes objectives quickly with the W but has almost no answer to a contested smite fight.","invade":"Walk into Morgana's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Morgana is very weak to an early invade, since Black Shield stops the crowd control and not the damage.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Dark Binding is the whole threat; sidestep it and she has a slow zone and a shield, neither of which kills you.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Morgana's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Morgana is weakest away from her laners, where the binding has no follow-up and the ultimate has no second target.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Morgana does not side lane; she plays beside a carry, where the shield turns a 2v2 into a 2v1.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Morgana picks are a binding from fog into her team, so cross the river outside her range or with a body between.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Morgana wins by making one fight near her team unwinnable — a shield on the right person and a root on the wrong one."},"Taliyah":{"tldr":"Taliyah adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Taliyah seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Taliyah attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Taliyah into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Taliyah's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) introduces an immense cross-map initiation mechanic that provides an unstoppable dive and massive area-of-effect fear. Execute a precise ultimate activation from fog of war to crash into Taliyah or their laner for a clean kill. This massive mechanical spike turns you into an absolute map-wide playmaker threat who dictates the shape of every fight through global dives."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Taliyah's first item makes the volley-into-shove combo a real burst instead of chip damage from range."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Taliyah clears fast with Threaded Volley but is squishy, and you beat her at level 1 and by a wide margin at 2 and 3. Start on the buff facing hers and walk in at level 2. Unraveled Earth scatters rocks that explode if you dash over them, and Head Rush counts as a dash, so walk around the minefield before you jump. Seismic Shove (900 range, 14-second cooldown) knocks you back and ends your frenzy, so bait it first. Take scuttle whenever she rotates mid, and recall after the invade.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Taliyah is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Taliyah contests scuttle at range with the volley and the shove rather than by standing on the crab.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Taliyah if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Taliyah has good objective damage but a poor pit fight, so contest her smite attempts rather than racing them.","invade":"Walk into Taliyah's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Taliyah is weak to an early invade, since Seismic Shove is her only escape and it needs to land to work.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Worked ground is visible — she does far less damage on it, so fighting on ground she has already used is safer.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Taliyah's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Taliyah is weakest at close range with the shove spent, where she has no way to make distance again.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Taliyah shoves side waves and crosses the map on her passive, so she is rarely where the wave says she is.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Taliyah picks are a shove into her team or a wall behind you, so watch which direction she is facing before you cross.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Taliyah wins by splitting the map with Weaver's Wall and zoning the fight her team chooses to take."},"Zyra":{"tldr":"Zyra adjusts your early mechanical tempo by requiring high precision over Chilling Scream (E) defensive timing and Blood Frenzy (W) automation management. Briar completely commands skirmish velocities through unmatched lifesteal, using Head Rush (Q) to shred armor, and deploying Certain Death (R) to execute high-impact global dive initiations. Zyra seeks to out-scale your kit over 6-camp full clears, kite your frenzied approach vectors, and exploit your lack of health regeneration outside of combat.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Start with Blood Frenzy (W) to secure a fast automated clear, utilizing the recast bite to execute monsters and burst-heal. Execute the bite trigger precisely when the monster drops low to maximize your missing-health execution values. This establishes an exceptionally fast and healthy path across your starting camps."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Unlocking Head Rush (Q) provides an impactful targeted stun that shreds armor and enables powerful early dueling. If Zyra attempts an uncalculated early entry into your jungle, jump on them with Q before activating Blood Frenzy to automatically run them down. This completely secures your early map pressure and forces them to retreat immediately."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Absolute Peak","why":"Access to Chilling Scream (E) completes your lethal dueling portfolio by introducing a versatile damage reduction and wall-stun mechanic. Use this tool to instantly cancel your frenzy if dragged under a tower, or charge it to shove Zyra into terrain during deep jungle collapses. This grants unmatched flexibility allowing you to turn early brawls on both sides of the map."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Tempo Generation Focus","why":"Your basic abilities now hit severe early pressure thresholds, letting you dictate the entire tempo of map pressure through hyper-aggressive vertical invades. Keep constant tabs on Zyra's jungle clearing lines and use your automated frenzy to run them down inside dark jungle zones. Prioritize rapid champion kill generation and early skirmishes over executing slow, farm-heavy full clears."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Domination","why":"Certain Death (R) gives you a long-range global initiation and a fear on arrival, but it grants no CC-immunity — Zyra's Grasping Roots (E) can root you the instant you land at 1100 range, and Stranglethorns (R) knocks you up if she has it up. Time the cast from fog of war onto an isolated target rather than assuming you're untouchable once you arrive. This is your biggest mechanical spike and turns you into a real map-wide threat, not an unstoppable one."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Sundered Sky / Eclipse Spike","why":"Completing your core item triggers a massive physical damage and sustained fighting multiplier that completely overpowers traditional brawlers or isolated targets. Zyra's first item is where plant damage stops being chip and starts removing a squishy health bar in one rotation."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"High-Impact Diver","why":"Briar transitions into a high-impact skirmish diver who relies entirely on landing Certain Death and surviving the initial burst with Chilling Scream. Your late-game raw damage scaling shifts into a purely dive-focused line, making it imperative to coordinate with your team before frenzying into the enemy backline. Maintain extreme technical precision around high-tier objective pits to cleanly fear the contesting smiter and secure the objective."}],"start":"Zyra clears fast with plants doing the work, and you beat her at level 1 and by a wide margin at 2 and 3. Open toward her jungle and invade at level 2, before her seeds are placed around her camps. Blood Frenzy locks onto the nearest enemy, prioritising champions, so it goes past her plants to reach her. Grasping Roots (1100 range, 11-second cooldown) roots you out of the chase, so Head Rush in after it misses. Kill seeds before they grow if you fight near them. Scuttle is yours unless seeds are already growing beside it; recall after the invade.","scuttle":"Secure the scuttle crab the moment it spawns, using your Q stun to instantly drop its resistance shield and establish river control. Avoid soloing early Dragons unless Zyra is explicitly confirmed dead or visible ganking top lane on the other side of the map. Zyra contests scuttle on seeds — a crab fight over a grown plant garden is one she wins without duelling.","topObj":"Force the fight for early Void Grubs the exact moment they spawn, using your frenzied area-of-effect damage to clear them rapidly. Use your Q to stun Zyra if they contest, catching them off-guard mid-clear. Zyra melts objectives with plant damage but has no way to survive a pit fight she does not control.","invade":"Walk into Zyra's jungle the moment you confirm they are engaged with a low-health camp. Cast your Head Rush to stun them before activating Blood Frenzy to secure an inescapable duel. Zyra is very weak to an early invade away from her seeds, since the kit has no escape at all.","watch":"Watch for sudden counter-invades if you exhaust your Chilling Scream early while clearing a camp. This leaves you with nothing defensive left or frenzy-canceling tools to execute a clean escape. Seeds on the ground are the whole warning — kill them on sight and her damage drops by more than half.","weak":"When your side lanes lose priority, play defensively by abandoning contested scuttle crabs and using wards to safely trace Zyra's routes. Funnel entirely into creating pick opportunities in opposite lanes where your Certain Death can guarantee a cross-map kill. Zyra is weakest with no seeds down and her root on cooldown, which is when she has nothing at all.","split":"You cannot split push safely due to your lack of targeted escapes, meaning you must group to look for massive Certain Death dive opportunities. Avoid front-on standard engagements where your frenzied model can be easily kited into towers or heavily crowd-controlled before you enter your healing threshold. Zyra does not side lane; she plays near her team where the plants and the knock-up cover a choke.","picks":"Focus entirely on hunting for isolated targets or clustered enemies by launching your Certain Death from across the map. In standard group fights, look to execute a clean cross-map dive, using your ultimate's massive fear to instantly disrupt their formation directly and completely shattering their backline carriers. Zyra picks are a Grasping Roots through a choke into a seeded garden, so never walk a corridor she has covered.","win":"Generate an unanswerable mid-game map-wide gold lead through successful global ultimate dives and secure absolute early epic neutral priority. Close the match by relentlessly chaining frenzied takedowns in decisive mid-game skirmishes before the enemy carries scale enough to burst through your healing. Zyra wins by covering an objective choke in plants and ending any fight taken inside it with the knock-up."},"Locke":{"tldr":"Locke is a weak-side execute jungler: he loses honest duels and farms for the totem — fight him marks-zero, punish every spent blink, and never coin-flip at sliver HP inside Purgatory.","stages":[{"stage":"Level 1 Clear","adv":"Briar Favored","why":"Locke clears at range but pays mana and HP for it — his level 1 duel is honest only with nail marks banked, so fight him marks-zero. Head Rush (Q) into Blood Frenzy (W) closes the gap before he can bank a Ritual Nails mark to consume."},{"stage":"Level 2 Skirmish","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"His E is engage AND escape in one button: the ten seconds after his blink are your whole trade window. Jump him with Head Rush (Q) the second Ashen Pursuit is on cooldown and he has no way out."},{"stage":"Level 3 Route","adv":"Briar Dominant","why":"Full kits online — sidestep the Q recasts and his burst never adds up; your all-in with Blood Frenzy (W) has no half-measure once you're locked onto him."},{"stage":"Levels 4-5 Macro","adv":"Even — Farm & Track","why":"Levels 4-5 vs Locke are a tempo war — he wants quiet farm into his 6; tax his camps, keep his marks off you at contests, and bank the gold lead his weak duel hands you."},{"stage":"Level 6 Breakpoint","adv":"Certain Death Favored","why":"Purgatory executes anyone who fights below the floor inside his totem — disengage above ~15% or leave the zone entirely. Outside the totem, Certain Death (R) picks the target and Blood Frenzy finishes it — your all-in has no half-measure."},{"stage":"First Item Spike","adv":"Lich Bane / Shadowflame Spike","why":"His Lich Bane spike is real: the blink-consume chunk one-shots chipped squishies. Respect the first-item window, then note his E is still a one-way door — punish every spent blink. Locke's first item makes the mark consume hit for a real chunk, which is when the blink stops being a poke tool."},{"stage":"2+ Items Scaling","adv":"Briar Favored at Full Build","why":"Late-game Locke scales with his seal count, not his items — deny executes and his floor never rises. Focus him when E is down and never let \"almost dead\" linger inside Purgatory."}],"start":"Locke wants to fight from range with Ritual Nails, and a Briar that reaches him wins at levels 1 and 2 and by a wide margin at 3. Clear toward his side and walk into his raptors at level 3, where fresh Ritual Nails marks on the camp show he was there. Ashen Pursuit (10-second cooldown) teleports him before the dash, so wait for him to use it before you Head Rush. Soul Ignition damages him and heals some back at the end, so frenzy onto him while it is running. Take both scuttles, and recall once his raptors are gone and he has spent his flash.","scuttle":"Take the first scuttle contact with confidence unless you’re carrying 2-3 nail marks — his blink-consume needs stacks, so an unmarked contest is yours. Locke contests scuttle on his mark count, not his health bar — an unmarked contest is much safer than a stacked one.","topObj":"Contest grubs and herald hard pre-6; post-6, watch the totem drop — leave the pit above the execute floor and re-enter when it expires. Locke takes objectives adequately and the Purgatory totem makes a late pit fight far more dangerous than the numbers suggest.","invade":"Invade the side he shows opposite — his escape is one blink on a ten-second timer, and a Locke who spends E on a camp is a kill waiting for a ping. Locke escapes an invade with one blink on a ten-second timer, so an invade into a spent Ashen Pursuit is close to free.","watch":"Watch your own mark stacks like a cooldown: a stacked nail string into the blink-through consume deletes half a health bar — drop stacks before they mature. Watch your own mark stacks like a cooldown — a full nail string into the blink consume takes half a health bar.","weak":"If he executes a lane early, respect the seal — his floor just rose permanently. Deny the snowball by matching his ganks cross-map rather than duelling into his counter-window. Locke is weakest in the seconds after his blink is spent, when he is a ranged champion standing in melee range.","split":"He punishes greedy splitters with totem duels — send answers in pairs or shove the opposite side; solo brawls at low HP are exactly the fight he farms. Locke side lanes well because the totem punishes anyone who answers him at anything less than full health.","picks":"His picks start with a nail string from fog — hug vision lines, and treat three stacks plus his E up as a dive threat even at even HP. Locke picks start with a nail string from fog, so hug vision lines and treat three stacks as a dive threat.","win":"Win the duel war he keeps declining: invade the spent-blink windows, end fights above his floor, and starve the seal count that his whole late game is built on. Locke wins by raising his execute floor with every seal until low-health fights inside his totem stop being survivable."}};
